AI
==

Small proofs of concept while reading about artificial intelligence.
One directory per idea, each with the algorithm and a test that runs it,
nothing shared between them on purpose: they are meant to be read one at
a time.

Python needs nothing but the standard library, the C++ ones only a
compiler and make. The cuda ones want the toolkit and a card, but their
tests run without one and skip the parts that need it.

    python test_<name>.py     in a python directory
    make && ./<name>_test     in a c++ directory

Contents
--------

    annealing     simulated annealing for the travelling salesman
    antcolony     ant colony optimisation, same problem
    astar         A* path finding over a grid
    cudakmeans    k means with the assignment step on the gpu
    cudamatmul    matrix product on the gpu, naive and tiled
    fuzzy         fuzzy controller with triangular sets
    genetic       genetic algorithm for the knapsack
    hopfield      hopfield network as associative memory
    id3           decision tree by information gain
    kmeans        k means clustering
    knn           k nearest neighbours
    levenshtein   edit distance and a did you mean lookup
    linreg        linear regression, gradient descent and least squares
    markov        markov chain text generator
    minimax       tic tac toe solved by minimax
    mlp           multilayer perceptron trained with backpropagation
    naivebayes    naive bayes spam filter
    nqueens       n queens by backtracking
    perceptron    the perceptron learning rule
    qlearning     q learning on a grid world
    sudoku        sudoku solver
    viterbi       viterbi decoding for a hidden markov model
